      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): suppress unhandled rejection from async abort callback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe agent session extension abort callback calls void this.abort() without .catch(). The abort method is async and calls await this.agent.waitForIdle() which can reject. If it does, the unhandled promise rejection crashes the process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd .catch(() => {}) to suppress the unhandled rejection.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore: void this.abort() - async handler without catch - unhandled rejection - crash\nAfter: void this.abort().catch(() => {}) - rejection suppressed\n\n## Risk\n\nLow. One .catch(() => {}) addition.",
